# The elaborator's door (notes/elaborate.md "What it reads and writes"): `wap wap/extensions/theory/elaborate/door.wap
# program.wap` reads a program as it is written, the arguments, levels and types it leaves out found, and takes its
# statements in order. A declaration is elaborated, checked by the kernel and added, and nothing is said of it;
# `type of e` prints e's type, `axioms of name` the axioms it rests on. The first refusal is printed as its one line and ends the run with a failure.
use "../environment.wap"
use "read.wap"
use "file.wap"

file_elaborated(Theory(), args#1)
